109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Downtime in retail environments causes immediate financial leakage and irreparable damage to the customer experience. Currently, the resolution of Point- of-Sale \(POS\) software crashes relies heavily on manual intervention by checkout staff or remote IT support teams. This manual troubleshooting process is characterized by significant latency. A cashier must first identify that the application has frozen, alert a store manager, and then either attempt a hard reboot or wait for a support ticket to be resolved. During this window, which can span from several minutes to hours, checkout lines grow stagnant, frustrated customers abandon their purchases, and the store suffers direct revenue loss.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Furthermore, most retail edge devices operate in a technical vacuum, lacking the sophisticated automated orchestration layers found in enterprise-grade data centers. While tools like Kubernetes provide self-healing for cloud-hosted microservices, standalone retail terminals are often left vulnerable without any automated safety net. There is an urgent, critical need for a lightweight, localized 'self-healing' mechanism that can provide enterprise-level high availability on standard, standalone retail terminals. This project addresses the gap between enterprise cloud reliability and localized hardware reality, providing a cost-effective automation layer that safeguards the retail environment from the costs of technical failure.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
