123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (The architecture of the AI Self-Healing Cloud utilizes an advanced Asynchronous Multi-Threaded approach to ensure absolute operational decoupling and system stability. The software is constructed as a monolithic Python script for ease of deployment, but is logically split into two primary execution pathways. The Primary Thread hosts the WSGI Flask Server and manages the lifecycle of full- duplex WebSocket handshakes. This thread remains dedicated to networking, ensuring that store managers can always access the health dashboard regardless of how hard the backend is working.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (Concurrently, a Secondary Daemon Thread operates the infinite monitoring and simulation loop. This thread is configured with the daemon=True flag to ensure it is safely terminated by the OS when the host process stops. Within this loop, the script continuously queries the host kernel for target process IDs \(e.g., the POS executable\). If the process is missing, it triggers the healing protocol. Following the health check, the thread generates stochastic retail transaction data using Python's random module to simulate a live environment. This data is then simultaneously committed to the SQLite disk file and pushed into the shared memory state. Finally, the updated state is broadcasted to the frontend via WebSockets, allowing the Chart.js library to render live updates on the dashboard canvas.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
