/P 69 0 R
/E (5.2 Software Requirements)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (The host environment must execute a modern desktop operating system such as Windows 10/11 or a standard Linux distribution. The application requires a Python 3.8+ runtime environment. Core library dependencies include Flask for the web backend, Flask-SocketIO for telemetry streaming, psutil for cross-platform OS process management, and pyautogui for simulating human hardware interactions. To ensure the self-healing daemon remains active and starts automatically upon boot, it must be granted administrative privileges through the host's native Task Scheduler or Cron services.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (5.1 Hardware Requirements)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (The system is specifically engineered for edge deployment on localized retail hardware, requiring minimal overhead to maintain maximum performance. The minimum specifications include a standard x86/x64 or ARM-based processor \(2.0 GHz dual-core recommended\) and at least 4GB of system RAM. These resources are sufficient to host both the Python monitoring daemon and the primary retail applications simultaneously. For data integrity, a standard Solid State Drive \(SSD\) is required to ensure low-latency relational database commits during rapid automation cycles. No specialized server infrastructure or external cloud instances are necessary, as the terminal functions as a fully autonomous edge node.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (7)
